      "name": "",
      "role": "assistant",
      "text": "That is good to hear, and well done for not sharing anything.\n\nHere is what I need you to know. As long as you did not share any codes, PIN or card details, your money is safe, and the caller knowing you are a customer does not mean your card is compromised.\n\nScammers often call customers pretending to be the bank. Their goal is to make you panic, so you will hand over a one-time password or transfer money. You did exactly the right thing by hanging on to your details.\n\nIf you would like extra peace of mind, I can note this as a suspicious contact and help you monitor it. Would you like me to do that?",
